li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/gyojeong-dogam"><span class="enc-name">Gyojeong Dogam</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gyojeong Dogam, or Directorate General for Policy Formulation, was the office through which the Choe military house ruled the Korean kingdom of Goryeo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gyorgy-dozsa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gyorgy-dozsa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">György Dózsa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">György Dózsa was a Székely soldier from Transylvania chosen to lead a crusade against the Ottomans proclaimed in Hungary in 1514.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/gyptis"><span class="enc-name">Gyptis</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Gyptis is the daughter of Nannus, king of the Segobrigii, in the foundation legend of Massalia (Marseille).</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gytheio"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gytheio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gytheio</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Gytheio is a port town in Laconia, southern Greece, on the Laconian Gulf at the entrance to the Mani peninsula.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gyujanggak"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gyujanggak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gyujanggak</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gyujanggak was the royal library and research institute founded by King Jeongjo in 1776 at Changdeokgung palace in Seoul.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gyula-andrassy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gyula-andrassy